From: dyxushuai <dyxushuai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: resolve macvlan output devices

PPPoE sessions can use a macvlan device to provide an independent MAC
address. The flowtable forward path stops at macvlan because it does not
implement ndo_fill_forward_path, so the redirect action presented to the
Airoha PPE driver refers to the macvlan device instead of the underlying
GDM device.

Resolve the macvlan lower device before selecting the PPE output port. The
flow rule still carries the macvlan source address, so the generated PPE
IPv4 entry keeps the PPPoE session identity while targeting the physical
GDM port.

IPv6 PPE entries select their source address from UPDMEM using the physical
GDM port ID instead of storing the address in the flow entry. Reject IPv6
offload when the output is a macvlan until its address can be assigned to a
dedicated UPDMEM slot. This avoids frames using the physical GDM MAC.

Signed-off-by: dyxushuai <dyxushuai@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/ip.h>
+#include <linux/if_macvlan.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
 #include <linux/of_platform.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -359,10 +360,19 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(
 					int l4proto, u8 dsfield)
 {
 	u32 qdata = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, 0x7f), ports_pad, val;
-	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
+	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port;
 	struct airoha_foe_mac_info_common *l2;
+	bool is_macvlan = netdev && netif_is_macvlan(netdev);
 	u8 smac_id = 0xf;
 
+	if (is_macvlan && type >= PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV6_ROUTE_3T)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+	if (is_macvlan)
+		netdev = macvlan_dev_real_dev(netdev);
+
+	dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
+
 	memset(hwe, 0, sizeof(*hwe));
 
 	val = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATE, AIROHA_FOE_STATE_BIND) |
